    "trading_allowance_raise": {
      "description": "Candidate measure. From 6 April 2027 the trading allowance, which relieves trading receipts in place of actual expenses, rises from £1,000 to £3,000, for income tax and Class 4 National Insurance. Every self-employed person gets it: the data cannot tell a new venture from an established one. Without gross receipts in the data, a profit within the allowance is treated as fully relieved, so the cost may be overstated.",
      "display": "before-after",
